  "description": "<div>\n  <p>Each pile in <code>piles</code> contains bananas. In an hour, Koko chooses one pile and eats up to <code>speed</code> bananas from it; she cannot switch piles during that hour. Find the smallest positive integer speed that finishes every pile within <code>h</code> hours.</p>\n  <p>A partly eaten pile can be revisited later. Judge a proposed speed by adding the hours needed for every pile.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> piles = [3,6,7,11], h = 8\n<strong>Output:</strong> 4</pre>\n  <p>At speed 4 the piles require 1, 2, 2, and 3 hours.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> piles = [30,11,23,4,20], h = 5\n<strong>Output:</strong> 30</pre>\n  <p>One hour per pile requires speed 30.</p>\n  <p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n  <pre><strong>Input:</strong> piles = [30,11,23,4,20], h = 6\n<strong>Output:</strong> 23</pre>\n  <p>Speed 23 needs exactly six hours.</p>\n  <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><code>1 &lt;= piles.length &lt;= 1000</code>.</li>\n    <li><code>1 &lt;= piles[i] &lt;= 1,000,000,000</code>.</li>\n    <li><code>piles.length &lt;= h &lt;= 1,000,000,000</code>.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>",
